#ROOM
Vnum     51000
Name     Drakken Proxima Academy~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     You have arrived at Drakken Proxima Academy, a training station in orbit above
Proxima Centauri b. This academy teaches the basic commands needed to survive,
travel and interact with other people in the wider interstellar community.
Each compartment has a specific lesson. Explore the academy in full and read
each room carefully. The student message area is to the west; return here
afterward and continue north when you are ready.

The entrance concourse reflects its builders: armored radiation shutters,
heat-resistant plating and compact defensible passages. Through the nearest
observation panel you can see Proxima Centauri b below and the fierce red
primary beyond the shielded glass.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51001
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51130
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51001
Name     Drakken Instruction Spine~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor links the academy's first instructional rooms. The language and
communication lesson is to the west, while practical skill instruction is to
the east. When you have finished with both rooms, return here and continue
north.

The passage is built around armored radiation shutters, heat-resistant plating
and compact defensible passages, with deep red and neutral-white lamps chosen
to remain clear during emergency conditions. Displays along the wall present
Drakken survival oaths, expedition plaques and records of frontier
settlements.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51003
Desc      The Laboratory of Skills.
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51000
Desc      Entrance to Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51006
Desc      Abbigayle's Language Lessons.
~
#ENDEXIT

#MUDPROG
Progtype  leave_prog~
Arglist   100~
Comlist   if isimmort($n)
else
  mpforce $n vis
endif
~
#ENDPROG

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51002
Name     Drakken Navigation Success Annex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You completed the navigation exercise successfully. Continue north to return
to the reference room and resume the academy course.

A small window in this quiet annex looks toward Proxima Centauri b, a reminder
that the entire training complex is an orbital station.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51003
Name     Drakken Skills Laboratory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This is the academy's practical skills laboratory. Type PRACTICE to see the
abilities currently available to you. Your list may include weapon skills,
general skills, languages and other advanced abilities. To improve something,
use PRACTICE <full skill name>.

For example, to practice dual wield, type PRAC DUAL WIELD. Additional
proficiency is gained through training and successful use. Type HELP PRACTICE
or HELP <skill> whenever you need more information.

Drakken instructors favor a hard Drakken survival doctrine centered on
durability, aggression and preparedness. The room itself is equipped with
ruggedized systems protected against radiation, thermal swings and power
interruptions.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51040 1 51003
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51004
Name     Drakken Reference Archive~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors silence~
Desc     This quiet reference room suppresses most public channels so that students can
read without interruption. Type CHAN for a list of channels. You can disable a
channel with CHAN -<channel>, enable it with CHAN +<channel>, or use CHAN -ALL
and CHAN +ALL to silence or restore them together.

When you are ready, go west for the navigation exercise. Follow the room
descriptions until you find your way back here. If you become lost, the up
route returns you to this room. Once you have completed the exercise, continue
north.

The archive contains Drakken survival oaths, expedition plaques and records of
frontier settlements. deep red and neutral-white lamps chosen to remain clear
during emergency conditions keeps the room comfortable for long periods of
study.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51014
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51007
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51005
Name     Drakken Combat Trials Control~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors safe~
Desc     This chamber is reserved for controlled combat trials. In ordinary play you
will encounter mobiles, often shortened to MOBS. Some may be aggressive and
attack as soon as you enter their location. Defeating opponents can provide
experience and loot.

After a fight, EXAMINE CORPSE and GET ALL CORPSE can be used to inspect and
recover items. CONFIG +AUTOLOOT and related configuration options can automate
parts of this process. REST, SLEEP, WAKE and STAND are useful while recovering
between exercises.

The chamber is arranged around a hard Drakken survival doctrine centered on
durability, aggression and preparedness, with armored radiation shutters,
heat-resistant plating and compact defensible passages protecting the rest of
the station from the training area.
~
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51006
Name     Drakken Language and Culture Suite~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     This room teaches the language system. Type PRACTICE to see languages
available to you. Your native tongue and the common language are normally
available without additional study. To learn another language, use LANGUAGE
LEARN <language>.

For more information use HELP LANGUAGES, HELP SPEAK and HELP TONGUE. Language
study consumes practice sessions, and capable students generally learn more
efficiently.

The walls carry Drakken survival oaths, expedition plaques and records of
frontier settlements, giving students examples of how language, history and
identity developed among the Drakken.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51001
Desc      A Stone Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51094 1 51006
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51007
Name     Drakken Orientation Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is the beginning of the navigation exercise. Type CONFIG +AUTOEXIT if you
want obvious exits displayed automatically. EXIT lists visible routes, and
LOOK <direction> lets you inspect an adjoining direction before moving.

Your next route is west. Try EXIT and LOOK WEST before moving on. The exercise
uses armored radiation shutters, heat-resistant plating and compact defensible
passages to make each section visually distinct without changing the station's
underlying layout.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51009
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy, it looks safe
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51008
Name     Drakken Combat Practice Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This is a controlled combat practice bay. A restrained training creature is
used here to demonstrate attacking, judging an opponent and withdrawing from a
fight. The CONSIDER command compares your character with a potential opponent;
elsewhere, use CON <MOBNAME> before attacking something unfamiliar.

The bay follows a hard Drakken survival doctrine centered on durability,
aggression and preparedness. Heavy barriers and ruggedized systems protected
against radiation, thermal swings and power interruptions keep the exercise
isolated from the inhabited sections of the station.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51016
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51045 1 51008
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51009
Name     Drakken Sealed-Access Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This section teaches doors and less-obvious exits. A closed door may not be
listed among obvious exits until you interact with it. Read the room
description, LOOK <direction>, try moving into a direction, and use OPEN
<direction> or OPEN DOOR when appropriate. HELP OPEN provides more detail.

deep red and neutral-white lamps chosen to remain clear during emergency
conditions and deliberately repetitive wall panels make the exercise depend on
observation rather than decoration.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51010
Desc      An Enclosed Room
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51007
Desc      Wandering the Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51011
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51009 0 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a solid oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51010
Name     Drakken Discovery Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     You found the enclosed chamber. Hidden or closed rooms like this appear
throughout the game, sometimes with obvious clues and sometimes with very
subtle ones. LOOK, EXIT and careful reading are your most reliable tools.

The compact chamber uses armored radiation shutters, heat-resistant plating
and compact defensible passages. Its plain construction is intentional: the
lesson is to notice access routes rather than rely on elaborate scenery.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51009
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51010 2 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51011
Name     Drakken Hidden-Route Passage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This passage introduces special and hidden exits. Hidden routes may not be
found simply by walking into every wall. Read descriptions, inspect mobiles
and objects, and look for words that might identify a door or route.

Locked exits may require a key or an appropriate skill. Directions can be
abbreviated as N, E, W, S, NE, NW, SE, SW, U and D. Some special routes use a
word such as LEAVE, CLIMB or ENTER. Continue north and use the next room's
description to find the concealed route.

The Drakken design language here uses armored radiation shutters,
heat-resistant plating and compact defensible passages, making small visual
details especially important.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51012
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51009
Desc      Wandering Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51012
Name     Drakken Heritage Salon~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This chamber has been furnished as a Drakken heritage salon. A broad table and
twelve seats dominate the center while exhibits of Drakken survival oaths,
expedition plaques and records of frontier settlements line the walls. One
wall display appears slightly different from the others.

Use LOOK <word> on details mentioned in the room. Sometimes inspecting one
object reveals the clue needed to discover a hidden exit. The exercise is
unchanged mechanically; only the station's cultural presentation differs.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51011
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51013
Desc      door
~
Keywords  tapestry door~
Flags     isdoor closed secret~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51012 3 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    tapestry~
ExDesc       Upon closer inspection you realise that this is not even a tapestry, but
a cunningly camouflaged wall! You can see the outline of a door as you
look closer.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    west~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall here, something just isn't right about it.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    w~
ExDesc       You see a tapestry on the wall.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see a cleverly disguised door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    Crystal globes~
ExDesc       This globes cast shadows in the corners. The shadows on the west
tapestry almost appears to be an opening.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51013
Name     Drakken Maintenance Alcove~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     You found the concealed alcove. Secret rooms can contain useful items, clues
or alternate routes, so careful reading often pays off. This room also
demonstrates a special SOMEWHERE exit. Inspect the picture and nearby wall if
you want to discover the intended route, or use the obvious up exit to return.

The alcove exposes ruggedized systems protected against radiation, thermal
swings and power interruptions, giving the space the feel of a hidden service
compartment inside Drakken Proxima Academy.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51012
Desc      Lost in Darkhaven Academy
~
Keywords  door~
Flags     isdoor closed~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      Back to the beginning
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction somewhere~
ToRoom    51002
Keywords  crack~
Flags     hidden auto~
#ENDEXIT

Reset D 0 51013 1 1
#EXDESC
ExDescKey    door~
ExDesc       You see an oak door.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    picture~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    crack~
ExDesc       This is a huge CRACK, you could probably squeeze through it. 
~
#ENDEXDESC

#EXDESC
ExDescKey    wall~
ExDesc       This is a picture of fresh cut flowers in a glass vase. It seems to
be hanging here just to cover a huge crack. That crack is so large, you
can probably squeeze through it! Perhaps you should look closer at the
crack. HINT: type CRACK.
~
#ENDEXDESC

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51014
Name     Drakken Readiness Concourse~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     This corridor introduces commands used to inspect your character. SCORE shows
core statistics, EQUIPMENT lists worn items, INVENTORY shows carried items,
and LEVEL reports advancement information. Common abbreviations include SC, EQ
and I.

Use HELP <subject> for additional information. The concourse is finished with
armored radiation shutters, heat-resistant plating and compact defensible
passages, and deep red and neutral-white lamps chosen to remain clear during
emergency conditions clearly marks the route toward combat training.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51015
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51004
Desc      The Reading Room
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51015
Name     Drakken Combat Briefing Deck~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Combat training is immediately ahead. You can begin an ordinary fight with
KILL <mob>, while many learned skills and abilities can also initiate combat.
Before attacking unfamiliar opponents, use CONSIDER and review the help for
your available abilities.

Remember that aggressive actions against another player can have consequences.
The briefing deck reflects a hard Drakken survival doctrine centered on
durability, aggression and preparedness; ruggedized systems protected against
radiation, thermal swings and power interruptions monitors the practice bay
below.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51017
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51014
Desc      A Marble Corridor
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    51016
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51016
Name     Drakken Withdrawal Training Bay~
Sector   inside~
Flags    nomob indoors~
Desc     This bay explains ways to leave a dangerous fight. WIMPY can automatically
withdraw you when your hit points fall below a chosen threshold. FLEE attempts
an immediate manual withdrawal. Emergency recall or extraction mechanics may
also exist, but they generally carry a greater cost and should be treated as a
last resort.

The room is intentionally austere, with armored radiation shutters,
heat-resistant plating and compact defensible passages and clear route markers
designed to make emergency instructions easy to understand.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51008
Desc      A Dank Pit
~
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51015
Desc      Preparing for combat
~
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51017
Name     Drakken Recovery Lounge~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Long fights and long journeys require recovery. REST is the safest ordinary
way to recover. SLEEP can recover more deeply but leaves you vulnerable in
unsafe locations. Use WAKE after sleeping and STAND after resting.

Characters can also become hungry or thirsty. Ask the service unit here for
food or a canteen, then use EAT <item> or DRINK <item>. The fountain can also
be used directly or to refill a container.

This is a functional rest hall with heated seating and emergency gear built
into every wall. Beyond the windows lies Proxima Centauri b below and the
fierce red primary beyond the shielded glass.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51027
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    51015
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 51015 1 51017
Reset M 0 51065 1 51017
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51018
Name     Drakken Object Interaction Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Some items that initially appear unimportant can become useful later. Speak
with the student here and pay attention to what they have found.

Containers can hold other objects. Use LOOK IN <container>, GET <item> FROM
<container>, PUT <item> IN <container>, and OPEN <container> when necessary.

Hint: say hello. The exercise occupies a small Drakken student annex fitted
with ruggedized systems protected against radiation, thermal swings and power
interruptions.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    51022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51042 1 51018
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51019
Name     Drakken Fabrication Loft~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Some objects are obtained by manipulating, combining or crafting other
objects. Your character may eventually learn specialized crafting skills;
other situations are as simple as opening a container or operating a control.

This compact fabrication loft is dense with ruggedized systems protected
against radiation, thermal swings and power interruptions. It mirrors the
practical working style found throughout Drakken Proxima Academy.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    51022
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 51018 1 51019
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51020
Name     Drakken Salvage Exercise~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A common way to acquire equipment is to recover it from defeated mobiles.
After defeating the training unit here, use EXAMINE CORPSE to inspect what it
carried and GET ALL FROM CORPSE to recover the contents. Configuration options
can automate looting or currency collection.

The salvage exercise takes place in a reinforced work cell equipped with
ruggedized systems protected against radiation, thermal swings and power
interruptions and arranged according to a hard Drakken survival doctrine
centered on durability, aggression and preparedness.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    51022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51060 1 51020
  Reset E 1 51001 1 8
  Reset E 1 51002 1 13
  Reset G 1 51004 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51021
Name     Drakken Academy Supply Exchange~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors safe~
Desc     Shops are useful for acquiring equipment and selling items you no longer need.
LIST shows a merchant's stock, BUY <object> purchases something, SELL <object>
offers an item for sale, and VALUE <object> asks what the merchant will pay.

The backpack is particularly useful because it can hold spare equipment. This
supply exchange is decorated with Drakken survival oaths, expedition plaques
and records of frontier settlements and uses ruggedized systems protected
against radiation, thermal swings and power interruptions for inventory and
transaction handling.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 51070 1 51021
  Reset G 1 51017 1
  Reset G 1 51011 1
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     51022
Name     Drakken Equipment Acquisition Lab~
Sector   city~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Finding better equipment is an important part of progression. Some methods
become available only after learning the appropriate skills, including SEARCH
and DIG. Other methods may carry legal or social consequences.

The rooms east, west, above and below demonstrate different ways to obtain
useful items. Explore all four, then continue north.

This equipment lab uses armored radiation shutters, heat-resistant plating and
compact defensible passages; lockers and work surfaces are sized and arranged
for Drakken trainees.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    51023
#ENDEXIT

#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    51020
#ENDEXIT

